{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UFGZUKT6Tp17VJzNd3fYch","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd061-sleep\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/sleep: Pause for a Specified Duration\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Shell scripts use sleep to introduce delays between commands, in retry loops, and in\n6\t  polling intervals. The macOS BSD sleep accepts only integer seconds, while GNU sleep\n7\t  supports fractional seconds and multiple arguments (summed). The Go implementation must\n8\t  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gsleep, installed by coreutils) in argument\n9\t  parsing and exit code behavior, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Pause execution for the specified duration.\n13\t  - G2: Support fractional seconds and duration suffixes (s, m, h, d).\n14\t  - G3: Support multiple arguments whose durations are summed.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Core sleep behavior\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: Must pause for NUMBER seconds when given a single numeric argument, then exit 0.\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: Must support fractional seconds (e.g., sleep 0.5 pauses for 500 milliseconds).\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: Must support suffix multipliers s (seconds, default), m (minutes, x60), h (hours, x3600), d (days, x86400). The suffix is case-sensitive and lowercase only.\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: When multiple arguments are given, must sum all durations and sleep for the total.\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Input validation and error handling\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: Must accept zero as a valid duration and return immediately with exit 0.\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: When no arguments are given, must print a usage error to stderr and exit 1.\n36\t      - R2.3:\n37\t          text: When a non-numeric or negative argument is given, must print an error to stderr and exit 1.\n38\t      - R2.4:\n39\t          text: \"Must support infinity (or inf) as a duration, sleeping indefinitely until interrupted.\"\n40\t\n41\t  R3:\n42\t    title: Signal handling and output\n43\t    items:\n44\t      - R3.1:\n45\t          text: Must not produce any output to stdout or stderr under normal operation.\n46\t      - R3.2:\n47\t          text: Must not read from stdin.\n48\t      - R3.3:\n49\t          text: When --help is the first argument, must print a usage message to stdout and exit 0.\n50\t      - R3.4:\n51\t          text: When --version is the first argument, must print version information to stdout and exit 0.\n52\t\n53\t  R4:\n54\t    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n55\t    items:\n56\t      - R4.1:\n57\t          text: Must exit 0 after sleeping for the requested duration.\n58\t      - R4.2:\n59\t          text: Must exit 1 when given invalid arguments (no args, non-numeric, negative).\n60\t      - R4.3:\n61\t          text: \"Differential tests must compare exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must use short durations (0 or 0.01) to avoid slow test execution.\"\n62\t      - R4.4:\n63\t          text: \"Tests must cover: zero duration, fractional seconds, suffix multipliers (s, m, h, d), multiple arguments summed, error on no args, error on invalid arg, and error on negative arg.\"\n64\t\n65\tnon_goals:\n66\t  - cmd/sleep does not implement signal-based early wake (SIGALRM or similar).\n67\t  - cmd/sleep does not report remaining time on interruption.\n68\t\n69\tacceptance_criteria:\n70\t  - id: AC1\n71\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/sleep 0; echo $? prints 0 immediately, matching gsleep.\"\n72\t    traces:\n73\t      - R1.1\n74\t      - R2.1\n75\t      - R4.1\n76\t  - id: AC2\n77\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/sleep 0.01 completes in roughly 10ms and exits 0, matching gsleep.\"\n78\t    traces:\n79\t      - R1.1\n80\t      - R1.2\n81\t      - R4.1\n82\t  - id: AC3\n83\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/sleep exits 1 with error when given no arguments, matching gsleep.\"\n84\t    traces:\n85\t      - R2.2\n86\t      - R4.2\n87\t  - id: AC4\n88\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/sleep abc exits 1 with error on stderr, matching gsleep.\"\n89\t    traces:\n90\t      - R2.3\n91\t      - R4.2\n92\t  - id: AC5\n93\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gsleep passes for all cases listed in R4.4.\"\n94\t    traces:\n95\t      - R4.3\n96\t      - R4.4\n97\t  - id: AC6\n98\t    criterion: \"cmd/sleep compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n99\t    traces:\n100\t      - R1.1\n101\t      - R1.2\n102\t      - R1.3\n103\t      - R1.4\n104\t      - R2.1\n105\t      - R2.2\n106\t      - R2.3\n107\t      - R2.4\n108\t      - R3.1\n109\t      - R3.2\n110\t      - R3.3\n111\t      - R3.4\n112\t      - R4.1\n113\t      - R4.2\n114\t      - R4.3\n115\t      - R4.4\n116\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"902c10be-f962-4cd5-9e06-bc61c65a1040","uuid":"71ae109e-e9bb-4a56-bcdc-5f4072bf3d17","timestamp":"2026-05-21T14:00:48.547Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5414/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd061-sleep.yaml","content":"id: srd061-sleep\ntitle: \"cmd/sleep: Pause for a Specified Duration\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts use sleep to introduce delays between commands, in retry loops, and in\n  polling intervals. The macOS BSD sleep accepts only integer seconds, while GNU sleep\n  supports fractional seconds and multiple arguments (summed). The Go implementation must\n  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gsleep, installed by coreutils) in argument\n  parsing and exit code behavior, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Pause execution for the specified duration.\n  - G2: Support fractional seconds and duration suffixes (s, m, h, d).\n  - G3: Support multiple arguments whose durations are summed.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Core sleep behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must pause for NUMBER seconds when given a single numeric argument, then exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must support fractional seconds (e.g., sleep 0.5 pauses for 500 milliseconds).\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must support suffix multipliers s (seconds, default), m (minutes, x60), h (hours, x3600), d (days, x86400). The suffix is case-sensitive and lowercase only.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: When multiple arguments are given, must sum all durations and sleep for the total.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Input validation and error handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must accept zero as a valid duration and return immediately with exit 0.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: When no arguments are given, must print a usage error to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: When a non-numeric or negative argument is given, must print an error to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"Must support infinity (or inf) as a duration, sleeping indefinitely until interrupted.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Signal handling and output\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must not produce any output to stdout or stderr under normal operation.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must not read from stdin.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: When --help is the first argument, must print a usage message to stdout and exit 0.\n      - R3.4:\n          text: When --version is the first argument, must print version information to stdout and exit 0.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 after sleeping for the requested duration.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when given invalid arguments (no args, non-numeric, negative).\n      - R4.3:\n          text: \"Differential tests must compare exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must use short durations (0 or 0.01) to avoid slow test execution.\"\n      - R4.4:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: zero duration, fractional seconds, suffix multipliers (s, m, h, d), multiple arguments summed, error on no args, error on invalid arg, and error on negative arg.\"\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/sleep does not implement signal-based early wake (SIGALRM or similar).\n  - cmd/sleep does not report remaining time on interruption.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/sleep 0; echo $? prints 0 immediately, matching gsleep.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R4.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/sleep 0.01 completes in roughly 10ms and exits 0, matching gsleep.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R4.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/sleep exits 1 with error when given no arguments, matching gsleep.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.2\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/sleep abc exits 1 with error on stderr, matching gsleep.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.3\n      - R4.2\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gsleep passes for all cases listed in R4.4.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/sleep compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":116,"startLine":1,"totalLines":116}}}
