r handling\n     - R2.1: zero duration → exit 0; R2.2: no args → error; R2.3: invalid/negative → error; R2.4: infinity support\n     - Non-goals: no signal-based early wake, no remaining time reporting\n\n   - `cmd/sleep/main.go` (existing, 98 lines)\n     - Already implements R1.1-R1.4 AND R2.1-R2.4 from a prior task\n     - Header claims: `Implements srd061-sleep R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.4`\n     - Key code for R2 requirements already present:\n       ```go\n       // R2.2: no args check (lines 40-43)\n       if len(args) == 0 {\n           fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"sleep: missing operand\")\n           os.Exit(1)\n       }\n       \n       // R2.3: invalid/negative handling in parseDuration (lines 89-95)\n       val, err := strconv.ParseFloat(s, 64)\n       if err != nil { return 0, err }\n       if val < 0 { return 0, fmt.Errorf(\"negative duration\") }\n       \n       // R2.4: infinity handling (lines 55-57 and 65-67)\n       if math.IsInf(total, 1) { select {} }\n       // In parseDuration:\n       lower := strings.ToLower(arg)\n       if lower == \"infinity\" || lower == \"inf\" { return math.Inf(1), nil }\n       \n       // R2.1: zero duration (lines 59-61)\n       if total > 0 { time.Sleep(time.Duration(total * float64(time.Second))) }\n       ```\n\n   - `cmd/sleep/sleep_test.go` (existing, 51 lines)\n     - Uses differential testing pattern with `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n     - Has `discardStderr` normalizer for error cases\n     - Already has tests for: zero (R2.1), no-args (R2.2), invalid-arg/negative-arg/empty-string (R2.3)\n     - MISSING: No test case for \"inf\" or \"infinity\" (R2.4)\n     - Full existing test file:\n       ```go\n       func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n           goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n           refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gsleep\")\n           if err != nil {\n               t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n           }\n           discardStderr := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n           tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n               {Name: \"zero\", Args: []string{\"0\"}},\n               {Name: \"fractional\", Args: []string{\"0.01\"}},\n               {Name: \"suffix-s\", Args: []string{\"0.01s\"}},\n               {Name: \"suffix-m\", Args: []string{\"0m\"}},\n               {Name: \"suffix-h\", Args: []string{\"0h\"}},\n               {Name: \"suffix-d\", Args: []string{\"0d\"}},\n               {Name: \"multiple-args\", Args: []string{\"0\", \"0\"}},\n               {Name: \"multiple-fractional\", Args: []string{\"0.01\", \"0.01\"}},\n               {Name: \"multiple-suffixes\", Args: []string{\"0s\", \"0m\"}},\n               {Name: \"no-args\", ExitCode: 1, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr}},\n               {Name: \"invalid-arg\", Args: []string{\"abc\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr}},\n               {Name: \"negative-arg\", Args: []string{\"-1\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr}},\n               {Name: \"empty-string\", Args: []string{\"\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr}},\n           }\n           testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n       }\n       ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the existing implementation already contains code for R2.1-R2.4\n   - Key gap found: test coverage for R2.4 (infinity/inf) is missing from `sleep_test.go`\n   - Challenge with testing infinity: can't do a standard differential test since both binaries would block forever. Need to either test that `inf`/`infinity` are accepted without error (perhaps with a timeout-based approach or by testing that the process starts correctly), or find another testing strategy.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive stitch task prompt with full project context, SRD det